  "compositor": "JoyOffice WGSL source-over composition of projected old/new slides and their transparent background/content parts, rendered offscreen on a native adapter. Submitted frames are read back for GPUI display and live video overlays. Morph renders editable shapes directly. The deterministic CPU raster remains the standalone CLI default.",
  "budgets": {
    "maxImageAndReadbackMiB": 192,
    "maxLayers": 32768,
    "maxTriangles": 128000,
    "maxCoveredFrameMultiples": 96,
    "maxReadbackWaitSeconds": 5
  },
  "independentChecks": "Both graphics APIs compared every pixel against the deterministic CPU reference. The 64x36 CPU digest matches the archived pre-optimization compositor. Missing outgoing slide and missing parts are compared separately. Desktop captures converted from their display ICC profile to sRGB on macOS, sampled at 3,864 locations on each paused window, checked against the older CLI at the exact show clock with a one-sample neighbourhood.",
  "priority": "P2 D-GEOM",
  "rollback": "JOYDECK_GPU_TRANSITIONS=0 selects deterministic CPU composition in the same binary. Unsupported devices, live slide animation/GIF sources, over-budget frames and errors fall back to CPU.",
